  "text": "Surgery | Pet Emergency & Referral Center\nSkip to Primary Content\nBook\nContact Us\nMap\n3579 Northlake Blvd,\nPalm Beach Gardens,\nFL,\n33403\nCall\n(561) 691-9999\nEmergency\nEmergency\nPhone:\n(561) 691-9999\nAddress:\n3579 Northlake Blvd,\nPalm Beach Gardens,\nFL,\n33403\nEmployment\nOur Expansion\nCareers\nAbout Us\nAbout Us\nHours & Fees\nPayment Options\nPERC CARES Fund\nOur Team\nServices\nCritical Care\nEmergency\nInternal Medicine\nMedical Oncology\nSurgery\nClient Education\nClient Education Library\nFAQ\nHours & Fees\nUseful Links\nFor Veterinarians\nPatient Records & Referral Portal\nCase Studies\nOnline Pharmacy\nEmergency\nContact Us\nWe're open 24/7/365. Experiencing a pet emergency? Call\n(561) 691-9999\nSurgery\nSurgery isn't going to be required for all of the health problems that your pet may face. However, there are some conditions for which surgery is the best possible course of action\nSurgery isn't going to be required for all of the health problems that your pet may face. However, there are some conditions for which surgery is the best possible course of action, such as:\nBlockages\n: Your pet may develop a blockage and require surgery if they swallow something that they shouldn't have and it gets stuck.\nCancer\n: Depending on the severity of your pet's cancer, surgery may be necessary to remove some or all of their tumors.\nInjuries\n: Pets with severe broken bounds or wounds may need surgery for reconstruction or repair.\nTooth decay\n: If your pet needs to have their teeth removed due to gum disease or tooth decay, dental surgery will be required.\nSurgical Procedures We Offer\nOur hospital is ready to help you and your pets with a variety of surgical procedures. Some of the most common surgeries that we perform include:\nDental surgery\n: If your pet needs to have a tooth or oral growth removed, they will need dental surgery to do so.\nInjury repair surgery\n: If your pet has been seriously injured, they may require surgery.\nOrthopedic surgery\n: If your pet has a broken bone or severe arthritis, they may require orthopedic surgery to repair or correct the problem.\nRemoval of foreign bodies\n: If your pet has a foreign body lodged in their digestive tract, they may require surgery to remove it.\nSterilizations\n: If you need to spay or neuter your pet, they will require a sterilization surgery.\nTumor removal surgery\n: If your pet has a cancerous or painful tumor, they may require surgery to remove it.\nPet Emergency and Referral Center\n3579 Northlake Blvd\nPalm Beach Gardens\n,\nFL\n33403\nT:\n(561) 691-9999\nF:\n(561) 775-0094\nHours of Operation\nMain Hours\nMon\nOpen 24 hrs\nTue\nOpen 24 hrs\nWed\nOpen 24 hrs\nThu\nOpen 24 hrs\nFri\nOpen 24 hrs\nSat\nOpen 24 hrs\nSun\nOpen 24 hrs\nEmergency\nAbout Us\nOur Team\nServices\nHours & Fees\nContact Us\nTerms & Conditions\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility\nFAQ\nEmployment\nCookie Preferences\nDo Not Sell or Share My Information\n©\nCopyright\n2026",
